    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** serving as our primary offensive engine, boasting a strong 67.73 efficiency score. His matchup against Gray is the most favorable on our board; the 3.92 xERA of the opposing starter, combined with a significant +14% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage, positions **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to anchor our run production from the three-hole. While **Jackson Merrill** (57.82) and **Sam Antonacci** (56.09) face more formidable tasks against Gausman and Brown respectively, their optimal batting order placements provide enough categorical stability to warrant the start. We are exercising caution with **Drake Baldwin** (46.72) and **Miguel Vargas** (48.50), whose scores were dragged down by the elite SP skill of their opponents, S\u00e1nchez and Brown. Both remain in the lineup today, but they are playing closer to their floors than we would typically prefer.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding players like **Jordan Westburg** or **Heliot Ramos**, who were pushed out primarily due to our strict game-cap preservation strategy during this final stretch of the season. Given the scarcity of stolen bases in our 5x5 Roto format, we prioritize the speed-oriented profiles of our active starters over the fringe power upside of the bench. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL, alongside our core studs **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, all of whom are inactive today due to team off-days. With **Andy Pages**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Franklin Arias**, and **Henry Bolte** all currently sitting, we are effectively protecting our remaining games-played budget for the final push. Keep a close eye on the weather at the sites of our active games; any significant rain delays could force an immediate mid-day adjustment to these score projections.",
